# Goal: Verify button-chain behavior

## Current state and prior-goal handoffs

§ 2.1
This goal begins only after goal 01 completes and hands off button-chain.html with named user-visible button targets and .completion-message styling.

§ 2.2
During this planning-only proof, these checks are documented but not executed.

## Outcome and definition of done

§ 3.1
Prove the implemented page meets the required user story and non-browser static acceptance checks. Definition of done: the future executor has run the planned static inspection and direct browser story, recorded evidence, and confirmed no open UI bugs remain.

## Why this goal is needed

§ 4.1
The requested behavior is interactive and visual, so implementation is not sufficient without static acceptance checks and direct browser evidence.

## Scope

§ 5.1
Included: static artifact inspection for the single file and exact text contract, plus US-01 browser validation through direct clicks on rendered buttons.

§ 5.2
Excluded: changing production code, weakening acceptance criteria, using console or injected events, and declaring completion while any required UI story is untested or bug found.

## Affected files, systems, data, and interfaces

§ 6.1
Verification reads button-chain.html after implementation and writes evidence into plan artifacts. Browser validation opens the local file directly or through the project-approved local route if the executor chooses one later.

## Dependencies and handoffs

§ 7.1
Depends on W01, W02, W03, and W06 through W04. W05 depends on W04 so obvious static contract failures are caught before browser work.

§ 7.2
If W04 or W05 fails, execution must add bug investigation and fix goals before resuming completion work.

## Implementation approach, risks, and edge cases

§ 8.1
Run the cheapest discriminating proof first: inspect the artifact contract, then run the browser story from a fresh state and record decisive evidence.

§ 8.2
Risks include off-by-one terminal behavior, stale story cache after implementation selector changes, and accidental evidence from non-UI shortcuts. Invalidate the story cache if the implementation changes the user-visible targets.

## Owned work units

§ 9.1
`W04` — static artifact inspection confirms the single-file and exact-text contract before browser execution.

§ 9.2
`W05` — Run the direct browser story that clicks the current last button five times, confirms one button is appended when clicking the initial button and generated buttons 1 through 3, and confirms clicking generated button 4 clears the document and shows finished with a visible white border.

## Testing requirement

| Test required | Rationale |
|---|---|
| yes | This goal consists of verification work units that must record pass/fail evidence before execution can complete. |

